  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As the current lags the voltage, the circuit must contain a combination of resistance and inductance.</p><p>Power factor&nbsp;<math><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cos</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow></mrow></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><msqrt><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mtext>0.6</mtext></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mtext>0.6</mtext></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mtext>0.6</mtext></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>0.64</mtext></mrow><mtext>0.36</mtext></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.8</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.6</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now we want the power factor&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#981;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></p><p>This is the condition of resonance in which</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#969;C</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math></p>"
  }
